    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear Phil, I have three questions. </div><div>I&#39;m participating in a project that used a Guttman scale to assess a general aspect of child development. In the first analyzes, we have replaced all missing values by some logical value (e.g., if a specific child was able to perform a complex behavior, all precedent/easier behaviors were coded as &quot;yes&quot;; If we have three &quot;no&quot; in a row, all sequential values were coded as &quot;no&quot;. I wrote you a message in this same forum that time asking about M2 values and you were very helpful (as always!). Thanks much (<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/mirt-package/luis$20anuncia%C3%A7%C3%A3o%7Csort:date/mirt-package/YR-EgypzV_4/ElMKxuz1AQAJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!searchin/mirt-package/luis$20anuncia%25C3%25A7%25C3%25A3o%257Csort:date/mirt-package/YR-EgypzV_4/ElMKxuz1AQAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473102153000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3tm7eCfn-U0TjnejsCIQpL\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/mirt-package/luis$20anuncia%C3%A7%C3%A3o%7Csort:date/mirt-package/YR-EgypzV_4/ElMKxuz1AQAJ</a>). </div><div><br></div><div>However, In our current meeting, we decided to allow &quot;missing cases&quot;. In other words, now we are using all dataset without any replacement. (Please check the figure attached to this message).</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/attach/24f4f103352e3/mirt_missing.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1\" alt=\"mirt_missing.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"310\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\"></p><div><br></div><div>My first question is related to estimation. The Graded Model converges after 2 thousand iterations, but when I ask M2 statistics (and CFI, TLI, RMSEA), mirt gives me the following warning:</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Error</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">The</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> following items have only one response category </span><span style=\"color:#008\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cannot be estimated</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y1 y2 y3 y4 y5 y6 y7 y8 y10 y12 y13 y14 y15 y16 y17 y18 y19 y20 y21 y22 y23 y24 y25 y26 y27 y28 y29 y30 y31 y32 y33 y34 y35 y36 y37 y38 y39 y40 y41 y42 y43 y44 y45 y46 y47 y48 y49 y50 y51 y52 y53 y54 y55 y56 y57 y58 y59 y60 y61 y62 y63 y64 y65 y66 y67 y68 y69 y70 y71 y72 y73 y74 y75 y76 y77 y78 y79 y80 y81 y82<br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">In</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cov2cor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cross</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> outer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">colMeans</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> colMeans</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  diag</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(.)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> had </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">or</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA entries</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> non</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">finite result </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> doubtful<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Error</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Null</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model did </span><span style=\"color:#008\">not</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> converge </span><span style=\"color:#008\">or</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">not</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> supported</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>But these variables have three categories.  </div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cg_items$y1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">14</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">53</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div></code></div><div><div>I really don&#39;t know how to interpret that. Could you please give me some insights? I&#39;m able to ask the model coefficients though.</div></div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>In addition to that, I read in an old message that you said </div><div>&quot;Moreover; once my model is estimated, the only way to compute fit indices such as RMSEA, CFI etc... is to impute the original dataset using the function imputeMissing ? Is this apporach correct ?</div><div><i>Correct. I can&#39;t see any other way to do this because these statistics are based on complete datasets</i>&quot;. </div><div><br></div><div>So, <b>can I assume that all IRT estimation need to use complete dataset</b>? </div><div>Link here: <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/mirt-package/missing$20complete$20cfi%7Csort:date/mirt-package/slssi-7_koA/N-bghDqJBgAJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!searchin/mirt-package/missing$20complete$20cfi%257Csort:date/mirt-package/slssi-7_koA/N-bghDqJBgAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473102154000&amp;usg=AOvVaw287mdIs-uuswNPXMMAvnOM\">https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/mirt-package/missing$20complete$20cfi%7Csort:date/mirt-package/slssi-7_koA/N-bghDqJBgAJ</a></div><div><br></div><div><div><br></div><div>The third question is related to different results between mirt estimation and ltm estimation. <b>The correlation is negative (-.7) and I&#39;m having a hard time to understand that. </b></div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>The attached data is virtually the same I&#39;m using and the following code will make my question clear.</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit_mirt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cg_items</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> itemtype </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;graded&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> technical</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NCYCLES</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ltm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit_ltm </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> grm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cg_items</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">IRT</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">param</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>M2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit_mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;C2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> na</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>coefs </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">coef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit_mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">IRTPars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> simplify</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>coefs </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cbind</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">coefs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">coef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit_ltm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> standardized </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>cor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">coefs$items</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">coefs$Dscrmn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>Thank you for being so supportive of all the members of this forum.<br></div><div>Luis</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
